  "body": "Whether you're stepping onto the property ladder, expanding your investment portfolio, or searching for a low-maintenance home in a highly convenient location, this solid 1980s weatherboard residence presents an opportunity that's hard to overlook.\r\n\r\nPositioned on a single level for effortless everyday living, this well-maintained home offers three generously sized bedrooms, a functional family bathroom, and a practical layout designed to suit modern lifestyles. The light-filled living and dining areas create a warm and welcoming atmosphere, while the kitchen provides excellent functionality with plenty of storage and workspace.\r\n\r\nOutside, you'll appreciate the easy-care grounds that require minimal upkeep, leaving more time to enjoy life. A single internal-access garage provides secure parking and additional storage, while extra off-street parking offers flexibility for family members, visitors, or tenants. Ideal for someone wanting to park their boat which is just minutes from the Half Moon Bay Marina and boat ramp. \r\n\r\nLocation is where this home truly shines. Situated within easy walking distance to Pakuranga College, it is an ideal option for families wanting quality schooling close to home. Excellent public transport links are also just moments away, making commuting to the Auckland CBD and surrounding suburbs simple and convenient. Nearby shopping centres, parks, cafes, and everyday amenities complete the package, delivering a lifestyle of comfort and accessibility.\r\n\r\nFor first-home buyers, this is an affordable opportunity to secure a quality home in a sought-after East Auckland location. For investors, the combination of durable weatherboard construction, single-level living, strong rental appeal, and proximity to schools and transport creates an investment with broad tenant demand and excellent long-term potential.\r\n\r\nHomes offering this level of convenience, practicality, and value are always in demand. Don't miss your opportunity to secure this fantastic property.\r\n\r\nThe property is scheduled to go to auction on the Tuesday 1st December 2026 (unless sold prior) held at the Bucklands Beach Yacht Club from 6pm\r\n\r\nPlease contact Simon Davies on 021 535 280 for a private viewing or any questions.",
